@page "/legend"

<PageTitle>Legend</PageTitle>

<section class="legend-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Knowledge</p>
    <h1>Legend</h1>
    <p>
        Terms used on Ask, Status, and the
        <a href="/rag-pipeline.html">RAG flow</a> animation.
    </p>

    <h2>Pipeline</h2>
    <dl>
        <dt>RAG</dt>
        <dd>Retrieval-augmented generation: answer from found documents, not from the model’s memory.</dd>
        <dt>Ingest</dt>
        <dd>Load documents before anyone asks. Today: <code>.md</code> files under <code>data/seed/policy</code>.</dd>
        <dt>Chunk</dt>
        <dd>A short slice of a document, not the whole file.</dd>
        <dt>Embedding</dt>
        <dd>A list of numbers that represents meaning. Similar text sits close together.</dd>
        <dt>Index</dt>
        <dd>The store of chunks + embeddings. This prototype keeps it in memory in the Web process.</dd>
        <dt>Retrieve</dt>
        <dd>Embed the question and pull the nearest chunks.</dd>
        <dt>Generate</dt>
        <dd>The LLM (large language model) writes an answer using only those chunks.</dd>
        <dt>Policy</dt>
        <dd>C# rules after the model. Can Deny or send to a human even if the model said yes.</dd>
        <dt>Stub</dt>
        <dd>A stand-in when Ollama is offline. Not an LLM — word counts and copied sentences so the app still runs.</dd>
        <dt>Citation</dt>
        <dd>Which source file a retrieved chunk came from.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>This app</h2>
    <dl>
        <dt>Ingestion module</dt>
        <dd>Turns files into chunks + embeddings. Hosted inside Web.</dd>
        <dt>Assistant module</dt>
        <dd>Ask + Policy inside Web. Answers only from retrieved chunks.</dd>
    </dl>
</section>
